<title>RUSSIA: ING-Barings to recommend S&amp;P, Moody's to Irkutsk.</title>
<headline>ING-Barings to recommend S&amp;P, Moody's to Irkutsk.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING-Barings, the ratings consultant for Russia's Irkutsk region Eurobond, will recommend Standard &amp; Poor's and Moody's rating agencies to the local administration, an ING-Barings official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision will be taken by the local administration. Our recommendations will be S&amp;P and Moody's,&quot; Dmitry Kushayev, assistant director, corporate finance, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said the decision must be taken by the start of June</p>
<p>Irkutsk region in Siberia plans to issue $80 million of dollar-denominated Eurobonds in late 1997 or early 1998.</p>
<p>By the end of May Irkutsk will decide who will lead-manage the issue and Kushayev said ING-Barings had an advantage in the tender.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
